Dedicated to Professor Parimal K. Bharadwaj on the occasion of his $67^{t h}$ birthday
Proton conduction (PC) is one of the paramount property for biological organisms and energy conversion in electrochemical systems such as polymer electrolyte fuel cells.[1l Nafion and Nafion-like polymer membranes are efficient proton conductors,[2] however, the high costs and temperature limitations have driven a number of strategies towards the design of alternative materials, such as coordination polymers (CPs） and/or metal organic frameworks (MOFs)[3], covalent organic polymers (COFs).[4] Selfassembled and hierarchical polymeric structures are formed by the interactions of organic matrices and inorganic salts where crystal engineering plays significant role to design those solids[5] with specific physical properties such as proton conductivity through the formation of H-bonds networks. From this view point advance functional proton conducting materials were prepared by introduction of acidic organic linkers (e.g. -COOH, -SO3H，- $\mathsf{P O}_{3}\mathsf{H}_{2};$ ）onto the framework backbone,[6] intrinsic loading of additional protonic molecules (e.g., imidazole, histamine)[7] and incorporation of different protonic carriers[3a-c.6d,8] within the pores.
Templating (to get free carboxylates sites) small organic polycarboxylic acids into the coordination frameworks could be an effective approach for construction of template assisted proton conducting materials. The template molecules may act as framework support and/or charge balance moieties to their hosts. Although template approach has widely been utilized for constructions of zeolites, phosphates, sulfates and sulfides for different functionalities, it remains less studied in CP/MOF systems.[9] The templates can connect the adjacent coordination frameworks and control hydrogen bond networks to create effective PC pathways. On the other hand CPs constructed from rigid bridging ligand 4,4'-bipyridine (bpy)[10] can incorporate small guest anions (in the form of poly-carboxylate templates) to assist the overall charges through its positively charged metal-bpy chains.
Along this line, we report three $\mathsf{C o}(\mathsf{I I})$ -based CPs synthesized using bpy as organic linker bearing common $\begin{array}{r l}{{[\mathsf{C o}(\mathsf{b p y})(\mathsf{H}_{2}\mathsf{O})_{4}]^{2+}}}&{{}}\end{array}$ chains which are neutralized by templated polycarboxylates viz. furan di-carboxylate (fdc) in Co-fdc, benzene tricarboxylate (btc) in Co-tri and benzene tetra-carboxylate (btec) in Co-tetra with molecular formula $\{[\mathsf{C o}(\mathsf{b p y})(\mathsf{H}_{2}\mathsf{O})_{4}](\mathsf{f d c})\cdot(\mathsf{H}_{2}\mathsf{O})_{1.5}\}_{n},$   
$\{[\mathsf{C o}(\mathsf{b p y})(\mathsf{H}_{2}\mathsf{O})_{4}](\mathsf{H b t c})\cdot(\mathsf{H}_{2}\mathsf{O})_{1.5}\}_{n},$   
$\{[\mathsf{C o}(\mathsf{b p y})(\mathsf{H}_{2}\mathsf{O})_{4}](\mathsf{b t e c})_{0.5}{\cdot}\mathsf{H}_{2}\mathsf{O}\}_{n}$ respectively. These CPs adopt 1D architectures and exhibit excellent proton conductivity with the help of H-bonded networks by free templates and crystallized waters in the lattices. Maximum PC values obtained by the deprotonated entities viz. Co-fdc and Co-tetra are $4.85\times10^{-3}$ and $4.15\times10^{-2}\mathsf{S c m}^{-1}$ respectively under $80^{\circ}\mathsf{C}$ and $98\%$ R.H., whereas, a PC value of $1.49\times10^{-1}\mathsf{S c m}^{-1}$ under similar conditions has been realized for the protonated moiety i.e. Co-tri which stands highest among the proton conducting materials $(\mathsf{M O F s}^{[3,11]}$ and ${\mathsf{C O F s}}^{[4]},$ 。 Moreover, Co-tetra and Co-tri are excellent conductors at ambient temperature $(40\ ^{\circ}\mathsf{C})$ with the values reaching up to $10^{-2}$ $\mathsf{s c m}^{-1}$ . There have been steadily growing PC values in the above mentioned systems reported, and there are now a handful of materials that give PC values in excess of the $10^{-2}\mathsf{S c m}^{-1}$ [4,11]
Co-fdc, Co-tri and Co-tetra were crystallized by room temperature evaporation method. An aqueous solution of $C_{0}(N O_{3})_{2}\cdot6H_{2}O$ ，bpy, and respective polycarboxylic acids (fdcH2, btcH3 and btecH4) were stirred in hot condition and filtrates were kept for evaporation. The phase purity of the bulk samples were confirmed by powder X-ray diffraction (PXRD) (Figure S1-S3, SI).
Single crystal analysis showed that asymmetric unit of each CP contains positively charged $\mathsf{[C o(b p y)(H_{2}O)_{4}]^{2+}}$ unit and certain number of carboxylate anions in charge assist proportion (Figure S4-S6, Sl). All three CPs are 1D with similar type of distorted octahedral $[\mathsf{C o}(\mathsf{b p y})(\mathsf{H}_{2}\mathsf{O})_{4}]^{2+}$ entities in their repeating units. Templates in the frameworks control the alignment of 1D coordination chains and provide proton-conductive H-bond
