Low-temperature fuel cells[3] are recently receiving attention for their usage as parts of portable power devices because of the high power consumption associated with anhydrous proton conduction.Thus,we were interested to check the PC behavior at $40\ ^{\circ}\mathsf{C}$ and $98\%$ R.H. lmpedance analysis showed the conductivity values for Co-fdc, Co-tri and Co-tetra are $9.54\times10^{-}$ 4, $1.38\times10^{-2}$ and $2.92\times10^{-2}\mathsf{S c m}^{-1}$ respectively, suggesting Co-tri and Co-tetra as excellent proton conductors even at ambient temperature.
The Arrhenius plot of all three CPs showed a good linear fit and the activation energy $E_{a}$ was estimated to be as 0.40, 0.40 and $0.29\mathsf{e V}$ for Co-fdc, Co-tri and Co-tetra respectively from the impedance spectra recorded at $98\%$ R.H.between 40 and $80~^{\circ}\mathsf{C}$ (Figure 4). The value ensured that conduction mechanisms are only of the Grotthuss fashion $(0.1-0.4\ \mathsf{e V})$ and is quite reasonable in the  well-directed  H-bonded  networks.[14] The  vehicle mechanism may be ruled out as none of the CPs contain any long range proton transport species, instead local molecular motion like vibrations and rotations of templates and water molecules are possible.[14b] To understand the mechanism it was proposed that protons of water molecules present in the lattice experienced a push pull (Figure S29, Sl) effect by $\cos\circ^{-}$ groups which are hopping forward through the extensive hydrogen-bonded networks, formed by the high-density functional carboxylates from the free templates. This push pull effect is getting facilitated in humid condition in presence of diffused water molecules for all the
CPs and the additional protons on the protonated template $({\mathsf{H b t c}}^{2-})$ in Co-tri are efficiently transported by reforming the Hbonds and thus exhibiting its superprotonic conductivity (Figure S29, Sl). Such a cooperation between proton carriers and water for high conductivity has also been identified for many MOFs.[3a3cl Moreover, the highly symmetric arrangement of carriers (orthorhombic system for Co-tri; monoclinic for Co-fdc and Cotetra), Co-tri conducts protons efficiently and isotropically ultimately leading to a superprotonic conductivity.[15] It may be noted that in spite of having the lowest activation energy Co-tetra turned out to be a medium conductor among the three and thus lowest activation energy does not necessarily equate to highest conductivity since proton conductivity is a complex phenomenon and multiple factors that affects conductivity need to be considered all together which is recently demonstrated by Shimizu et al.[16a]
We anticipated conductivity value in the ascending order of Co-fdc<Co-tri<Co-tetra as the ionic conduction is directly proportional to the carrier concentration and efficiency of proton transport.[3b-c] A careful evaluation of asymmetric units of three structures revealed the presence of a full $\mathsf{f d c}^{2\cdot}$ ,a full Hbtc²-, and half btec4- units and thus, the number of proton carrier carboxyl groups are same (two) in Co-fdc and Co-tetra while an additional carrier is present in Co-tri.Moreover, unlike Co-fdc and Co-tetra, the partially protonated template Hbtc²-in Co-tri may facilitate the proton transport through formation of highly competent H-bonded pathway for enhanced conductivity. It is worth mentioning that each structure contains four coordinated water molecules in their asymmetric units. There is ample paradigm that metal enhances the acidity of its bound water molecules.[3d]
Recyclability is one of the key factors of a proton conductor forsuccessful execution in fuel cell technology. Thus, temperature-dependent recycle test (40 to $80\ ^{\circ}\mathsf{C};$ ）in conductivity measurements for all three CPs was carried out at $98\%$ R.H. It was observed that all CPs were consistent in PC measurements up to five successful runs and details were provided in supporting information (Figure S30-S32, SI).
Co-tri is among the highest proton conducting CP under high humid condition; besides, there are only a few MOFs/CPs that exhibit conductivities of order $10^{-2}\mathsf{S c m}^{-1}$ (Table S5, SI).[16] These include: functionalized UiO-66 framework $(\mathsf{U i O-}66(\mathsf{S O}_{3}\mathsf{H})_{2})$ [11a] showing a high conductivity of $8.4\times10^{-2}\mathsf{S c m}^{-1}$ at $80^{\circ}\mathsf{C}$ and $90\%$ R.H.; followed by Fe-CAT- $5^{[11\mathrm{c}]}$ 1 $\mathsf{^{\prime}}5.0\mathsf{\times}10^{-2}\mathsf{S}\mathsf{c m}^{-1}$ ， $25^{\circ}\mathsf{C}$ $98\%$ R.H.), $\{[(\mathsf{M e}_{2}\mathsf{N H}_{2})_{3}(\mathsf{S O}_{4})]_{2}[Z\mathsf{n}_{2}(\mathsf{o x})_{3}]\}_{\mathsf{n}}[11\mathsf{d}]$ $(4.2\times10^{-2}\mathsf{S}$ cm-1， $25^{\circ}\mathsf{C}$ ， $98\%$ R.H.), PCMOF- $\cdot10^{[11\mathtt{e}]}$ $(3.55\times10^{-2}\textsf{S}\mathsf{c m}^{-1}$ ， $70~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ $98\%$ R.H.) and ${\mathsf{P C M O F}}2_{1/2}$ $2.1\times10^{-2}\mathsf{S c m}^{-1}$ ， $85^{\circ}\mathsf{C}$ $90\%$ R.H.).[1fl Moreover, Cotri and Co-tetra are the only examples which could perform the excellent conductivity in order of $10^{-1}$ to $10^{-2}\ \mathsf{S\ c m}^{-1}$ within the temperature range from 40 to $80~^{\circ}\mathsf{C}$ ，
In summary, we have proposed a simple yet powerful template assisted strategy for synthesizing proton conducting coordination polymers where the templates remained in the frameworks with charge assist proportions. The rational synthesis route enabled to isolate a partially protonated template from completely deprotonated templates in the frameworks with varying number of ionic carriers and thus exhibiting exceptional
